NoteLearning objectives



By the end of this lecture you will be able to:

write the simple linear regression model and state its LINE assumptions;
fit the model in R and interpret the intercept and slope in context;
partition variability with ANOVA and interpret the MSE and \(R^2\);
test the slope with a t-test and the overall model with an F-test;
tell a confidence interval for the mean response apart from a prediction interval;
check the assumptions with residual diagnostics and influence measures.
